== Current identity assessment ==
The profile for the adult William named with children at Mid Calder in 1648 was merged into this profile on 27 September 2026. The same parish, compatible age and absence of a better identified William support one working identity. The 1609 christening, adult fatherhood in 1648 and other possible child entries retain their separate citations below; the connection between the child and adult is an inference rather than a statement in any one register entry. No citation or existing family link was discarded in the merge.

== Biography ==

'''William Glasgow''' was christened on 24 December 1609 at Mid Calder, Midlothian, Scotland. A derivative FamilySearch index names his father as '''Jhone Glasgow'''.<ref name="FS1609">"Scotland, Births and Baptisms, 1564–1950," database, FamilySearch, entry for William Glasgow, christened 24 December 1609 at Mid Calder, Midlothian, Scotland, father Jhone Glasgow; [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:X1B2-3LV FamilySearch record X1B2-3LV]. This is a derivative index; the original register image has not been examined for this profile.</ref>

The cited record does not establish William's exact birth date. No reliable evidence has yet been identified for his mother, spouse, occupation, death or burial. The man named as father of Johne and Issobel in the Mid Calder baptisms of 3 February 1648 is now represented in this profile. Identifying that adult father with the William christened here in 1609 is an evidence-based inference: the name, parish and adult chronology fit, and no stronger competing William has been identified. The children are documented for the adult in 1648, while the link to his 1609 christening remains uncertain.

== Research Notes ==

=== Christening and register coverage ===

Scotland's People advises that a baptism index may show a birth date, a baptism date or both without identifying which is displayed; the displayed date is more commonly the baptism date.<ref name="SPGuide">Scotland's People, "Church registers," particularly the guidance concerning baptism indexes and variable register contents; [https://www.scotlandspeople.gov.uk/help-and-support/guides/church-registers Church registers guide].</ref> The profile's birth year should therefore remain uncertain. The exact date 24 December 1609 belongs to William's christening, not to a proved birth.

Hardy Bertram M'Call's survey of the Mid Calder records reports that the baptism register begins in 1604, but mothers' names were not recorded until after 1707. The baptism register is blank from July 1649 to August 1651; marriage proclamations are blank from July 1649 to November 1659; and the proper death register begins only in 1783. The kirk-session record is likewise blank from August 1649 to August 1651.<ref name="MCallRegisters">Hardy Bertram M'Call, ''The History and Antiquities of the Parish of Mid-Calder, with Some Account of the Religious House of Torphichen, Founded upon Record'' (Edinburgh: Richard Cameron, 1894), pp. 245–246; [https://archive.org/details/historyantiquiti00mcal/page/245/mode/2up Internet Archive].</ref>

Consequently:

* The original 1609 entry should not be expected to name William's mother.
* Absence from the Mid Calder registers during 1649–1651 would not be negative evidence.
* An ordinary Mid Calder parish death-register search cannot establish William's seventeenth-century death.
* The original entry may still supply manuscript spelling, a residence or occupation for his father, witnesses and useful page context.

=== Father and possible sibling ===

The derivative 1609 index supports only a father named '''Jhone Glasgow'''. It does not identify that man with [[Glasgow-3608|John Glasgow]] or prove the dates, parents or other identity details presently assigned to that profile. If Glasgow-3608 is retained as the named-father profile, the relationship should be marked uncertain and his unsupported ancestry should not be treated as William's proved ancestry.

A separate derivative index entry from 1608 has been attached to [[Glasgow-1086|Jhone Glasgow]].<ref name="FS1608">"Scotland Births and Baptisms, 1564–1950," database, FamilySearch, entry for Jhone Glasgow, 1608; [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:X1BL-X8B FamilySearch record X1BL-X8B].</ref> He is a possible brother of William, but the two original entries must be compared before concluding that they name the same father.

=== Adult household and identity assessment, 1643–1655 ===

